WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.969
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.969 --> 00:00:11.256
We are joined by some of our
colleagues from Financial Aid,

00:00:11.256 --> 00:00:15.817
and so this is our chance
to really talk about that.

00:00:15.817 --> 00:00:20.010
And so, Elizabeth,
could you please introduce yourself and

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.519
tell us a little bit about your role?

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.540
&gt;&gt; Hi everyone, yeah,
my name is Elizabeth LIamas.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.330
I am the Associate Director of
Financial Aid here at the GSB.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.970
Very excited to be
joining you this morning.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.271
So I work with all students, veterans,

00:00:36.271 --> 00:00:39.792
everyone to help them through
the financial aid process, and

00:00:39.792 --> 00:00:43.198
then also support you while
you're a student with the GSB.

00:00:43.198 --> 00:00:43.926
&gt;&gt; Cool, so

00:00:43.926 --> 00:00:49.399
can you tell us a little bit about
what's financial aid like at the GSB?

00:00:49.399 --> 00:00:50.099
What's the process?

00:00:50.099 --> 00:00:55.891
&gt;&gt; Sure, so for most students,
we've built a system around three

00:00:55.891 --> 00:01:01.253
guiding principles that we want
to instill in our process,

00:01:01.253 --> 00:01:04.940
excellence, access, and fairness.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:09.571
And so when we talk about financial aid,
we do have a combination,

00:01:09.571 --> 00:01:12.315
in general, of fellowship and loans.

00:01:12.315 --> 00:01:16.011
And we're looking at a student's
income and assets which is, very,

00:01:16.011 --> 00:01:21.160
if you've been through a financial aid
process before which some of you may have.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:25.426
This is probably very similar,
something that you're familiar with.

00:01:25.426 --> 00:01:29.935
We have as far as the process goes,
we have our own financial aid portal for

00:01:29.935 --> 00:01:31.660
our students.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:38.500
So it's a one stop shop portal for
you that's customized to your situation.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.191
And it's a great tool for our students
to connect with our office but

00:01:42.191 --> 00:01:46.225
also to submit everything to us very
securely, so very excited about it.

00:01:46.225 --> 00:01:49.254
&gt;&gt; Cool, and
then knowing our audience today,

00:01:49.254 --> 00:01:53.877
can you tell us a little bit more
about opportunities for veterans and

00:01:53.877 --> 00:01:58.438
especially maybe can you touch on
Yellow Ribbon Program, please?

00:01:58.438 --> 00:02:03.394
&gt;&gt; Definitely that's probably chapter 33,
post 911 Yellow Ribbon

00:02:03.394 --> 00:02:08.360
is definitely one of the most common
VA benefits that we have at the GSB.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:14.074
And so for those who are maybe looking
to use their Yellow Ribbon benefits for

00:02:14.074 --> 00:02:17.538
the first time,
essentially once you're eligible and

00:02:17.538 --> 00:02:22.052
you receive your certificate of
eligibility you'll have 36 months.

00:02:22.052 --> 00:02:27.405
Our program is built around a 9
month financial aid budget, so

00:02:27.405 --> 00:02:33.610
you'll be using about 18 months for
the two years of your benefit.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:37.300
And Stanford is committed to
supporting our Yellow Ribbon

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.870
veterans as much as possible.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:44.130
So our match with the VA funding
will cover up to your tuition.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.710
So that's a really great thing for

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:51.380
our veterans that they don't have
to worry about the tuition costs.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:56.490
For those who maybe are not
Yellow Ribbon eligible, we still have,

00:02:56.490 --> 00:03:00.470
like I said other methods of financial
aid to help support you as well.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:06.349
&gt;&gt; Cool, and then what about folks who
might be interested in the nonprofit or

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:08.135
government sectors?

00:03:08.135 --> 00:03:13.144
&gt;&gt; Yeah, so, yeah, we have a, and I think
I know where you're going with this.

00:03:13.144 --> 00:03:17.735
We have a really awesome loan forgiveness
program if you do find that you need to

00:03:17.735 --> 00:03:21.156
borrow loans to help supplement
your educational costs.

00:03:21.156 --> 00:03:26.901
And so that's for students who are looking
to go back into a government sector or

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:30.320
possibly into the nonprofit sector.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:33.930
This program has been around at
the GSB for a very long time.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:37.420
So over ten years,
it's a well established program.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:38.290
It is our own,

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:43.400
it's completely independent from
the government's loan forgiveness program.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.680
And if you do enter into one
of these sectors essentially,

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:52.030
we will help you assist you repay
your loan balances as an alumni.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.530
So it's a really great opportunity for

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:59.462
those who are thinking about going back
into the nonprofit or public sector.

00:03:59.462 --> 00:04:05.029
&gt;&gt; Cool, and then as I'm thinking about
financial aid and prospective applicant,

00:04:05.029 --> 00:04:09.869
do you have any tips, best practices,
things that we should be keeping

00:04:09.869 --> 00:04:13.920
in the back of our mind as we're
going through the journey?

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:21.010
&gt;&gt; Definitely so Stanford's has
their own veterans department, OMAC.

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:23.383
I'm not sure if you've already touched
on that in the past section, okay.

00:04:23.383 --> 00:04:28.445
So we work hand in hand with OMAC, so
it's really important, as you start

00:04:28.445 --> 00:04:33.510
to get this information that you're
not only in communication with us but

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:39.220
we will also assist with communication
with the OMAC and come together.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:43.193
The earlier you can get your
documentation ready the better.

00:04:43.193 --> 00:04:47.151
So that's going through whatever
VA process that you need to,

00:04:47.151 --> 00:04:51.050
especially getting that
certificate of eligibility.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:55.300
And so if you need assistance as far as
the next steps, we definitely ask that you

00:04:55.300 --> 00:05:00.610
reach out to us or to our colleagues at
OMAC to assist you with that process.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.341
But other than that,
we're here to support you.

00:05:03.341 --> 00:05:07.425
So if you're admitted, we will walk you
through the necessary steps to apply for

00:05:07.425 --> 00:05:08.273
financial aid.

00:05:08.273 --> 00:05:13.076
&gt;&gt; Cool, so the OMAC that we referred
to a couple times as the Office for

00:05:13.076 --> 00:05:17.392
Military Affiliated Communities
at Stanford University.

00:05:17.392 --> 00:05:20.066
And this is not just a GSB organization,
but

00:05:20.066 --> 00:05:24.044
one that helps support our veterans
across our whole community,

00:05:24.044 --> 00:05:27.528
both the undergrads and
the different grad department.

00:05:27.528 --> 00:05:33.289
So once again, OMAC in the Office for
Military Affiliated Communities.

00:05:33.289 --> 00:05:37.839
Now, let's say I'm an admitted student,
is there any way to kind

00:05:37.839 --> 00:05:42.323
of understand what I could be
getting as a financial aid package?

00:05:42.323 --> 00:05:47.805
&gt;&gt; Yeah, so once you're admitted we do
have a calculator tool which we encourage

00:05:47.805 --> 00:05:53.122
all students to use to get a better
understanding of what they may qualify for

00:05:53.122 --> 00:05:57.160
before they begin
the financial aid process.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:06:02.604
So that will be available to
you as an admitted student.

00:06:02.604 --> 00:06:08.604
&gt;&gt; Cool, and then one other thing
knowing that kind of from experience,

00:06:08.604 --> 00:06:10.574
what about families?

00:06:10.574 --> 00:06:14.971
Oftentimes we think about, hey,
I'm applying to business school as

00:06:14.971 --> 00:06:19.963
an individual, but for many of our
applicants, there's either a significant

00:06:19.963 --> 00:06:24.901
other, or there's children who are
going to be participating in this journey.

00:06:24.901 --> 00:06:27.442
How does that factor into financial aid?

00:06:27.442 --> 00:06:32.175
&gt;&gt; Yeah, so our cost of attendance
which is essentially the budget for

00:06:32.175 --> 00:06:35.950
the program,
is built around your circumstances.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:39.890
So if you're single or if you're married,
and if you're married if you're bringing

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:43.795
any children or
dependents with you to the GSB.

00:06:43.795 --> 00:06:46.950
So, of course those costs may increase for
you.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:53.295
For our Yellow Ribbon recipients,
you are eligible for

00:06:53.295 --> 00:06:58.310
a housing allowance on top
of the tuition payment.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:03.451
So you would be receiving that monthly
as well to help offset those costs.

00:07:03.451 --> 00:07:07.733
&gt;&gt; Cool, thank you just we've
covered a lot of ground-

00:07:07.733 --> 00:07:09.203
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:07:09.203 --> 00:07:10.413
&gt;&gt; In actually really impressive

00:07:10.413 --> 00:07:11.067
amount of time.

00:07:11.067 --> 00:07:14.763
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Are there any other things that from

00:07:14.763 --> 00:07:19.824
you, having sat in your seat for so
long, any other words of wisdom or

00:07:19.824 --> 00:07:23.779
things that you would love
to share with the group?.

00:07:23.779 --> 00:07:28.844
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I mean it can be scary
approaching financial aid

00:07:28.844 --> 00:07:33.700
in general or
some people find it kind of stressful.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:35.487
The people in our office,
my colleagues and

00:07:35.487 --> 00:07:37.673
myself, we've been doing this for
a very long time.

00:07:37.673 --> 00:07:41.222
And I've also been a certified
official for the VA, so

00:07:41.222 --> 00:07:45.060
I know what you need to go
through to get your benefit.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:48.870
And so my tip to everyone is
just to start conversations

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:51.370
as early as possible with our office.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:55.958
We're here to assist you and we would love
to help you walk through this process and

00:07:55.958 --> 00:07:58.884
make sure that you feel
secure about your package and

00:07:58.884 --> 00:08:00.963
how you're going to afford the GSP.

00:08:00.963 --> 00:08:06.984
&gt;&gt; Nice, all right, so
those were my questions.

00:08:06.984 --> 00:08:10.531
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; If you can't tell there's a lot of

00:08:10.531 --> 00:08:14.351
joy in our office and we're going to
extend that joy to the group.

00:08:14.351 --> 00:08:17.033
We're going to open it up right now.

00:08:17.033 --> 00:08:20.674
Are there any general
financial aid questions or

00:08:20.674 --> 00:08:25.040
funding questions that folks
in the audience might have?

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:28.421
So feel free to pop those
into the Q&amp;A box, and

00:08:28.421 --> 00:08:35.005
let's really make the most of our time
with one of our financial aid experts.

00:08:35.005 --> 00:08:38.769
Again, my hands are pointing in this
direction because that's where her window

00:08:38.769 --> 00:08:39.555
is in my screen.

00:08:39.555 --> 00:08:43.343
I don't know where Elizabeth might
be on your screen so that might.

00:08:43.343 --> 00:08:46.683
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; But this is the time to ask.

00:08:46.683 --> 00:08:52.511
See if you have questions here.

00:08:52.511 --> 00:08:57.867
Here's a question from Krista, when is
the deposit for the program typically due,

00:08:57.867 --> 00:09:02.177
assuming you're admitted,
when do you have to make that deposit?

00:09:02.177 --> 00:09:07.367
&gt;&gt; Yeah, so the deposit is,
we'll jump in if [LAUGH] I believe deposit

00:09:07.367 --> 00:09:13.226
is due by the time that you accept your
admissions offer, is that correct?

00:09:13.226 --> 00:09:16.283
Great, so it's due upfront as just for

00:09:16.283 --> 00:09:21.473
once you had made it you'll have
to receive your financial award,

00:09:21.473 --> 00:09:27.696
really weigh your options and then commit
to the program and accept your offer.

00:09:27.696 --> 00:09:29.270
And that's when your deposit is due.

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:34.180
I will for the VA, with the VA
benefits the one thing that is not

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:39.477
covered if your post 911 eligible
is a deposit for our program.

00:09:39.477 --> 00:09:43.906
But you're still fully covered for
your tuition and

00:09:43.906 --> 00:09:49.048
the deposit will go to offset
other costs of the university.

00:09:49.048 --> 00:09:53.921
&gt;&gt; Great, all right, here's a question
about dual degree students.

00:09:53.921 --> 00:09:55.224
How is the GI Bill and

00:09:55.224 --> 00:09:59.608
the Yellow Ribbon benefits applied
towards dual degree programs?

00:09:59.608 --> 00:10:03.029
&gt;&gt; Yeah, so essentially,
with a dual degree program,

00:10:03.029 --> 00:10:08.045
you're looking at most likely a little
bit longer than an 18 month program,

00:10:08.045 --> 00:10:10.342
which is normal for an MBA student.

00:10:10.342 --> 00:10:14.428
So depending on the dual degree that
you're admitted to, it could be,

00:10:14.428 --> 00:10:15.596
24 months, etc.

00:10:15.596 --> 00:10:19.848
As long as you're,
enrolled in an educational program,

00:10:19.848 --> 00:10:24.550
that your VA benefits will continue
to support your education.

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:29.169
And so, like I had mentioned,
once you're eligible for Yellow Ribbon,

00:10:29.169 --> 00:10:33.937
you usually have, if you have not used
it before 36 months of benefits, so

00:10:33.937 --> 00:10:37.614
it's quite a bit of time and
we're only using about 18.

00:10:37.614 --> 00:10:40.709
So if your enrollment
extends past that 18 months,

00:10:40.709 --> 00:10:43.268
then you'll have continued eligibility.

00:10:43.268 --> 00:10:44.753
&gt;&gt; Great, thank you.

00:10:44.753 --> 00:10:48.166
Here's a really important
question from Carolyn.

00:10:48.166 --> 00:10:51.941
If you do not qualify for
Yellow Ribbon due to partial GI Bill,

00:10:51.941 --> 00:10:56.670
are there other financial aid programs or
scholarships that you recommend?

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:57.917
What's to that extent?

00:10:57.917 --> 00:11:03.034
&gt;&gt; Yeah, yeah, so if you're not eligible
for a VA chapter that covers your full

00:11:03.034 --> 00:11:08.564
tuition, then we encourage you to apply
for our Need-Based Fellowship Program.

00:11:08.564 --> 00:11:11.687
Which is what I talked about
a little bit in the beginning,

00:11:11.687 --> 00:11:14.350
where we look at your income and assets.

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:18.014
And you go through the process
like a normal student, and

00:11:18.014 --> 00:11:21.600
that, if your are eligible for
fellowship that can help

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:25.588
offset those additional costs
that are not covered by the VA.

00:11:25.588 --> 00:11:30.469
Additionally, we do have some resources
that you will have access to for

00:11:30.469 --> 00:11:32.235
external scholarships.

00:11:32.235 --> 00:11:35.371
And we definitely encourage all
of our students to look for

00:11:35.371 --> 00:11:38.123
additional opportunities
outside of our office,

00:11:38.123 --> 00:11:41.470
and we're also here to help
you with those opportunities.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:44.177
So we have a general list for
you to work off of.

00:11:44.177 --> 00:11:47.293
But there could be more
opportunities in that for you.

00:11:47.293 --> 00:11:50.249
&gt;&gt; Yeah, and Elizabeth,
correct me if I'm wrong, but

00:11:50.249 --> 00:11:50.960
last-
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:54.800
&gt;&gt; Wasn't the average
financial aid package around

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:57.824
$40,000 per year per student?

00:11:57.824 --> 00:12:01.956
&gt;&gt; Yeah, it was around $40,000 for
our students, and that's per year.

00:12:01.956 --> 00:12:06.820
So that can definitely help
supplement what the VA is giving you

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:08.577
towards the tuition.

00:12:08.577 --> 00:12:11.052
&gt;&gt; Great, here's the question.

00:12:11.052 --> 00:12:15.665
So the application process,
we're need blind in applications.

00:12:15.665 --> 00:12:20.641
So that means that how you're going to
finance your time at the GSB has no impact

00:12:20.641 --> 00:12:22.215
on the final decision.

00:12:22.215 --> 00:12:28.003
So our financial aid process
is need-based okay, so.

00:12:28.003 --> 00:12:30.522
&gt;&gt; Correct.
&gt;&gt; So a clarification there.

00:12:30.522 --> 00:12:34.595
For the applications, there's three
rounds, so round one, round two,

00:12:34.595 --> 00:12:36.290
round three.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:41.080
Is there a difference in financial
aid funding among the three rounds?

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:42.622
&gt;&gt; There's definitely not.

00:12:42.622 --> 00:12:47.461
We've committed that whatever round
that you're admitted to the GSB in you

00:12:47.461 --> 00:12:52.073
will have the same opportunity for
financial aid as those in round one and

00:12:52.073 --> 00:12:55.225
two versus three, or
any combination of those.

00:12:55.225 --> 00:12:59.345
So same opportunity,
any round you apply for you're admitted

00:12:59.345 --> 00:13:02.790
you still have the financial aid
opportunities as everyone else.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:05.735
&gt;&gt; Great and
here's one a little bit about housing.

00:13:05.735 --> 00:13:09.595
So, knowing that this-
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:13:09.595 --> 00:13:11.849
&gt;&gt; Financial aid covers a lot of ground

00:13:11.849 --> 00:13:16.960
here, is the housing stipend you mentioned
with Yellow Ribbon different than or

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:21.470
in addition to the housing allowance
received while using the GI Bill,

00:13:21.470 --> 00:13:22.790
do happen to know?

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:24.104
&gt;&gt; No, it's the same.

00:13:24.104 --> 00:13:27.397
So it's the BAH housing allowance
as part of the GI Bill,

00:13:27.397 --> 00:13:30.428
and it's going to be based
on Stanford's zip code.

00:13:30.428 --> 00:13:33.598
So if you're interested,
you can head over to the VA website.

00:13:33.598 --> 00:13:37.372
Our zip code is 94305.

00:13:37.372 --> 00:13:42.675
And you can check out what your benefit
level will be with the BAH housing siphon.

00:13:42.675 --> 00:13:45.545
&gt;&gt; Great, and
then one question here, actually,

00:13:45.545 --> 00:13:48.347
there's a couple questions
along this theme.

00:13:48.347 --> 00:13:53.396
So need-based financial aid,
can you talk a little bit more about what

00:13:53.396 --> 00:13:58.206
are a couple of the elements there and
then is it based only on those?

00:13:58.206 --> 00:14:02.610
What happens if there's something in
my life that isn't captured there?

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:07.197
&gt;&gt; Yeah, so the intial application
is going to ask you for

00:14:07.197 --> 00:14:11.375
several years of income
as well as your assets.

00:14:11.375 --> 00:14:15.892
And when we talk about assets, we
are looking at liquid and illiquid assets.

00:14:15.892 --> 00:14:17.580
And then we always leave,

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:21.820
we want to take a holistic approach
to your financial aid package.

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:26.176
And so we're opening it up to if you have
a circumstances that you think impedes

00:14:26.176 --> 00:14:28.420
your ability to pay for your education,

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:31.796
we definitely want to hear about
those in your application.

00:14:31.796 --> 00:14:35.690
So we have an opportunity for
you to explain and if for

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:39.675
some reason you have
extenuating medical expenses or

00:14:39.675 --> 00:14:44.770
possibly are supporting your family,
we want to know about those.

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:46.541
So there's an opportunity for

00:14:46.541 --> 00:14:50.091
you to explain situations outside
of what we're asking for.

00:14:50.091 --> 00:14:56.833
&gt;&gt; All right, so thank you again,
Elizabeth, for jumping on and helping.

00:14:56.833 --> 00:15:00.299
That was a lot of really helpful,
meaty information.

00:15:00.299 --> 00:15:02.380
&gt;&gt; It was a lot.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:07.230
And for those who have been asking
questions, thank you for your engagement.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:10.711
If you didn't get your
questions answered live today,

00:15:10.711 --> 00:15:15.671
we're going to continue answering some of
them over the course in the Q&amp;A box as to

00:15:15.671 --> 00:15:18.060
the best of our abilities.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:22.800
Also, feel free to jump on our website,
I keep referring folks back to that.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.325
It's going to be one of
your best resources.

00:15:24.325 --> 00:15:26.350
Continue asking us questions there.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:29.675
We are here to support
